cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LIMULUS-eVTOL: digital twin, preregistered reinforcement learning campaigns and run records"
message: "If you use LIMULUS-eVTOL in academic work, please cite the software through its DOI, and where relevant the manuscript whose results you rely on."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Mete"
    family-names: "Cantekin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6990-6340"
    email: "metecantekin@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Nisantasi University, School of Civil Aviation, Aircraft Maintenance and Repair Department; Istanbul Beykent University, Graduate Education Institute, Computer Engineering"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Orfeomete/limulus-evtol"
abstract: >-
  Digital twin and complete experimental record of a modular electric vertical takeoff and landing
  design with four independently tilting rotor modules and three constrained variants. Contains the
  six-degree-of-freedom dynamic model, a Gymnasium learning environment, a PPO implementation, a
  classical cascade reference controller, the preregistration documents of every campaign with their
  frozen decision rules, and the training logs and policy checkpoints of one hundred and forty-four
  runs in fourteen run directories. Every number reported in the two accompanying manuscripts can be
  regenerated from the scripts archived here, which are byte-identical to the versions that produced
  them.
keywords:
  - eVTOL
  - reinforcement learning
  - digital twin
  - preregistration
  - learning environment design
  - reproducibility
  - flight control
